 "content": "# Noisy-grid motif copies\n\nUse this branch when a distinctive single-color motif appears amid zeros and another background color. Record the motif's colored-cell offsets from its bounding box and search for translated copies whose motif positions all contain zeros. Recolor those matching positions with the motif color. Preserve every other cell, including the original motif and zeros/background at non-motif positions inside the bounding box. Do not assume flood-fill or neighbor propagation: test motif translations when the grid looks like noisy background plus one seed object. Consider rotations or reflections only if demonstrations support them."
}

