 "content": "# Periodic diagonal stripes\n\nUse this branch when sparse colored markers lie on a zero field and demonstrations suggest the output fills the grid with periodic diagonal bands. Identify the line invariant: constant row−column for down-right diagonals, or row+column for down-left diagonals. With zero-based coordinates, `column−row` indexes the phase for down-right stripes and `row+column` for down-left stripes; verify the sign against observed output. Infer the smallest plausible period by checking which candidate periods avoid assigning different colors to the same residue, and use demo outputs to establish the complete phase-to-color mapping. Color every cell from its phase, not just the marker positions. Verify cells on each demonstrated line and reproduce every demo; do not assume marker positions alone establish every residue's color."
}

